description:
Change under review. Task: give the model-list request a timeout so a provider that never answers cannot hang `models list`. Use the existing `requestTimeout` setting and the existing `withTimeout` helper.

Added files are shown in full. For changed files, only the changed region is shown; the rest of the file is unchanged and compiles.

`src/config/schema.ts` (unchanged, shown for context):
```ts
17 export const ProviderSettingsSchema = z.object({
18   /** How long to wait for a provider response, in seconds. */
19   requestTimeout: z.number().int().positive().default(30),
20   baseUrl: z.string().url().optional(),
21 });
```

`src/util/timeout.ts` (unchanged, shown for context):
```ts
4 export type TimeoutError = { type: "TimedOut"; afterMs: number };
5
6 export function withTimeout<T>(promise: Promise<T>, ms: number): ResultAsync<T, TimeoutError> {
7   const timer = new Promise<never>((_, reject) => setTimeout(() => reject(ms), ms));
8   return ResultAsync.fromPromise(Promise.race([promise, timer]), () => ({ type: "TimedOut", afterMs: ms }));
9 }
```

`src/providers/fetch-models.ts` (changed, lines 10-14):
```ts
10 export function fetchModels(client: ProviderClient, settings: ProviderSettings): ResultAsync<Model[], FetchModelsError> {
11   return withTimeout(client.listModels(), settings.requestTimeout).mapErr(
12     (cause): FetchModelsError => ({ type: "ProviderTimeout", cause }),
13   );
14 }
```

